<article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl text-gray-700">
  <.header>
    Privacy
    <:subtitle>What this demo stores about you: very little.</:subtitle>
  </.header>

  <div class="card space-y-8 p-6 leading-[1.65] sm:p-8">
    <section aria-labelledby="privacy-data">
      <h2 id="privacy-data" class="about-subheading">No personal data</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        There is no sign-up. Everyone uses the same shared demo account, so the app never asks
        for your name or e-mail address. Products, transactions and settings you change are sample
        data and are visible to every other visitor.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="privacy-cookies">
      <h2 id="privacy-cookies" class="about-subheading">Cookies</h2>
      <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
        <li>
          <code>_clothing_store_key</code>: the session cookie that keeps you logged in and protects forms against forgery.
        </li>
        <li>
          <code>_clothing_store_web_user_remember_me</code>: set only when you tick "Keep me logged in".
        </li>
        <li>
          <code>welcome_seen</code>: remembers that you have seen the welcome dialog, so it doesn't open on every visit.
        </li>
        <li>
          <code>theme</code>
          and <code>locale</code>: the colour theme and the language you picked in the header, for a year.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-2">
        All of them either make the app work or remember a choice you made. There are no tracking,
        advertising or analytics cookies.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="privacy-logs">
      <h2 id="privacy-logs" class="about-subheading">Server logs</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        The web server logs each request (IP address, time, requested page, referrer and
        browser) to protect the demo against abuse and to count visits. The logs rotate
        automatically and are never shared.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="privacy-reset">
      <h2 id="privacy-reset" class="about-subheading">Nightly reset</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        Every night at {reset_time(@reset)} ({@reset.timezone}) the database is rebuilt from the
        sample data, which removes everything visitors changed during the day.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</article>
